course: dictionary
lesson: 10856
title: One short word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some short words mean different things in different places. Vi is one of them. In a maths or history lesson it is a number. In a computing lesson it is the name of a program. The words around it tell you which meaning to use.
explain: Roman numerals use letters. I is 1, V is 5 and X is 10. When a smaller letter comes after a bigger one, you add them: V and I make VI, which is 5 + 1 = 6. So «In chapter VI» means chapter six, not a word to read aloud.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If the clock has numbers like III, VI and IX on it, VI must be a number. If the sentence is about a text editor on a computer, vi is the program. Ask: does my meaning fit here?
fact: VI is the Roman numeral for 6.
fact: Roman numerals use letters: I = 1, V = 5, X = 10.
fact: On a Roman clock, III is 3, VI is 6 and IX is 9.
fact: Vi is a short name for an old text-editing program used by computer programmers.
fact: Vi can also be a short form of the names Violet or Vienna, or a fragment of a word in other languages.
exercise: «In chapter VI the Cheshire Cat talked to Alice.» What number does VI stand for here? | 10 | *6 | 1 | 5
exercise: A programmer says, «I edit my code in vi.» What is vi here? | The number 6 | *A text-editing program | A chapter in a book | A town in Austria
exercise: On a Roman clock, I = 1 and V = 5. What is V and I added together? | 15 | 4 | *6 | 9
test: «King Henry VI» was a king of England. What is VI in his name? | *A number, 6 | A short form of Violet | A fragment of a French word | A computer program
test: Liam reads «vi» in a travel guide about a city in Austria. What might it be short for? | Violet | *Vienna | The number 6 | A text-editing program
exam: In the sentence «In chapter VI the Hatter talked to Alice», what does VI mean? | Violet | A computer program | *Chapter six, the number 6 | Vienna
